Backport of libsdl-org/SDL commit 114aca172 ("Fix for iOS 27 no op on
statusBarOrientation", merged 2026-09-20, PR #16355) onto release-3.4.12.

iOS 27 made -[UIApplication statusBarOrientation] a no-op, and SDL's iOS
backend read it to decide whether the screen is landscape when sizing a
fullscreen window and its display modes. A session started with the
device already in landscape therefore opened a portrait-sized window
(Waddle issue #291). Upstream's fix reads the active window scene's
effectiveGeometry.interfaceOrientation instead, through a new
UIKit_GetInterfaceOrientation() helper, and this is that change with its
context adapted: the release branch has no #pragma deprecation wrappers
around the old calls, which is the only reason upstream's commit does not
apply as-is. The camera-backend hunk is omitted (SDL_CAMERA=OFF here).

Applied by Scripts/build-deps.sh after the SDL checkout. Drop this file
when SDL_TAG moves to a release that contains the upstream commit; the
build stops with an error if it no longer applies either way.

